    {
      "id": "claim_1acc600f238a472b8fa9d17f7ab478ef",
      "statement": "The container image is built from a two-stage Containerfile: a builder stage (registry.access.redhat.com/hi/go:latest) that runs `go build -o bin/rosa-trusted-actions-server ./cmd/server`, and a runtime stage pinned to registry.access.redhat.com/hi/core-runtime:latest@sha256:81280d7fd6afa7a3d2a6da2e90e545cf8e5d187c80a69b2a1c875fdcd731aaed (digest-pinned, not just the latest tag) that copies only the binary, exposes port 8080, runs as non-root user 1001, and entrypoints rosa-trusted-actions-server.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Containerfile",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:50c494a09f6b08bbaed9da3f2ca83672733ed7db7452a89a688f00161ce7cdbb"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_298a6b5d07c3453e9df66e7098649c8d",
      "statement": "The container's exposed port 8080 and /health endpoint are the same values the regional Terraform root's ALB target group uses for its health check, so changing either requires updating both the Containerfile/application and terraform/regional/alb.tf together.",
      "evidence": [
